            "method": "agent_mediated",
            "date": "2026-07-30"
          },
          "notes": "Re-audited backend/main.py fresh rather than trusting the ticket's '16' count: found 17 implicit-HTTP-200 except-blocks (all 76 except-Exception blocks reviewed; 30 are on_startup() bootstrap handlers and 2 are fire-and-forget Alpaca-sync best-effort blocks, correctly out of scope). All 17 fixed: 14 use the canonical {status,message} 500 envelope (conventions.md §13); 3 (/health, /health/detailed, /test/endpoints) keep their existing custom/simple shapes per conventions.md §11/§13.3's explicit health-endpoint envelope exemption, but still return HTTP 500 (not implicit 200) with no raw exception text. traceback.print_exc() added wherever missing. Existing ValueError->4xx branches and 200 success shapes left untouched. Discovered backend/main.py's own POST /test/endpoints handler is dead code (shadowed by backend/routers/test.py's router, included first). Did NOT file this to claude/backlog/backlog.md mid-sprint (execution_prompt.md §7 write-scope hard restriction: backlog.md may only be written at STEP 5.2 sprint close, for returned_to_backlog notes) - self-caught after an initial erroneous write via /backlog-add, which was reverted (git checkout --) before commit. Recorded here instead; candidate for filing via the proper channel (lessons_learnt_cycle.md Phase 3 §6.2, or a human-initiated /backlog-add) at sprint close or in a future session. 19 new regression tests added (tests/test_st04_implicit_200_error_paths_fixed.py); full backend suite (922 passed, 5 skipped) confirmed no regressions. Head of Engineering sign-off: agent-mediated, approved, independently re-ran the full test suite and re-audited the except-block count before approving."
        },
